{
 "id": "Year3000C07",
 "slug": "year-3000/c07",
 "chapter": "Our name",
 "topic": "What if you woke up in the year 3000?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "It takes you all day to reach the old city. Broken towers, green with plants, quiet as a library."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "The dot leads you to a metal door. On it, scratched by hand, is your family name."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "Inside, it's cold. There's a sleep pod. Exactly like yours."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "And it's switched on."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "The screen says: 'Asleep since twenty twenty-six. Wake date: today.' Mo Seven wipes the frost off the glass."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "And the face inside... is yours."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "Mo Seven's hand is shaking. There's a note taped to the glass, in your sister's handwriting. It says: 'One of you is the copy.'"
  },
  {
   "beat": "p8",
   "text": "So who woke up in the museum?"
  },
  {
   "beat": "p9",
   "text": "Is any of this real? The science is. Germs change faster than your body can learn them. A thousand years makes English almost unreadable. And thirty-two generations make nearly everyone family. The sources are in the description."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p10",
   "text": "What would you do first in the year three thousand? Tell me in the comments, and subscribe so you don't miss part two."
  }
 ],
